# Cryptic Trilobite: "This creature enters with X +1/+1 counters on it. Remove a +1/+1 counter from this creature: Add
# {C}{C}. Spend this mana only to activate abilities. {1}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature."
# Turn 1 it is cast for X=2 ({X}{X} is {4}) and enters with two counters. With every other source spent but Mox Jet, a
# counter removed - no {T}, so not held back by summoning sickness - gives {C}{C} that pays Aether Spellbomb's
# "{1}, Sacrifice: Draw a card" but not Karn, Scion of Urza's {4}, a spell (CR 106.6), though with the Mox and the {C}{C}
# its last counter would make there would be five mana. Turn 3 four untapped sources cast
# Karn (the control); turn 5 an Island pays its "{1}, {T}" and the counter it lost comes back.

